WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.672
The row number window function is useful when we need to rank duplicate candidates.

00:00:04.672 --> 00:00:08.552
The query first calculates a completeness score.

00:00:08.552 --> 00:00:15.467
It gives a point when useful fields such as name, email, phone, or address are populated.

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:20.417
Then the duplicate records are grouped using the normalized identity fields.

00:00:20.417 --> 00:00:23.987
Within each group, row number assigns a rank.

00:00:23.987 --> 00:00:26.742
More complete records come first.

00:00:26.742 --> 00:00:34.910
If completeness is tied, the query considers signup date, and then the identifier provides a stable final tie-breaker.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.837
The record with rank one is the preferred candidate according to this rule.

00:00:39.837 --> 00:00:43.802
Notice that SQL is not deciding which person is real.

00:00:43.802 --> 00:00:47.107
We are implementing a policy that we designed.

00:00:47.107 --> 00:00:52.506
Run the query and compare the completeness score with the survivor rank for the duplicate group.
